Forum posts are full of characters that mean something in Markdown. The renderer escapes the ones that would change the output, and only those.

# not a heading
#hashtag stays as it is
- not a list item
+ not one either
1. not an ordered list
1) and not this
> not a quote
    not an indented code block

--- not a rule ---
---
===

2 * 3 * 4 = 24, a_b_c, snake_case_name, *stars*, **more stars**, _underscores_, ~~tildes~~, `backticks`
[a link](https://example.com) and ![an image](https://example.com/x.png) and [a reference][1]
<div class="note">HTML</div>, <b>bold</b>, <!-- comment -->, a < b > c, &amp; &copy;
<https://example.com> and <alice@example.com>
| not | a | table |
| --- | --- | --- |
\ a backslash, C:\Users\alice, \*already escaped\*
:smile: @alice #general

[b]BBCode still works[/b] in the middle of it: [i]2 * 3[/i], [url=https://example.com/a_b]a_b[/url].
